module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_declared_container_type_is_checked_by_head_only

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }

data a_declared_container_type_is_checked_by_head_only: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_declared_container_type_is_checked_by_head_only" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: AtCeiling { rung: StructurallyGuaranteed, ceiling_reason: "a declared container application is judged at every type-argument position by v1.compiler.infer application_arguments_inhabitance through declared_type_inhabitance, refused on the real acceptance path at the let annotation, declared return, record-literal field and call argument; executed on srv2 at head 484cdd4c49ca (unit kh-q2-regen3, gunbc sha256 2cf14fff76ec0fa3f04ef35ba6be4b2926216a9b0afc0089c3679249b1e2bdd1, mirrors at first_generation_equal=true), test.claim.declared_container_argument_witness 13 of 13; a position holding an unsolved type variable stays undecided, and the mismatch stays writable" as NonEmptyStr } },

  receipts: [
    "**a declared container type is checked by its head only** (a value whose container type disagrees with its declaration at some type-argument position is accepted, because the declared-position judgment compares the container's head, or at most its first argument one level down).",

    "INVALID STATE: an Accepted program in which a binder, return, field or argument declared Map<K1, V1> (or List<List<A>>) holds a value of Map<K2, V2> (or List<List<B>>) with K1 /= K2 or V1 /= V2 (A /= B).",

    "HARM: silent wrongness. The emitted Rust drops the annotation (`let q: Map<Bool, Bool> = m` emits `let q = m.clone();`), so rustc has nothing to refuse either, and the wrong type surfaces at the first consumer that reads the value as its declared type.",

    "SPECIMEN (srv1, v1 seed built from main 8de219bdc5ad, 2026-10-30): `let m: Map<String, Int> = map_insert(empty_map(), \"a\", 1)` then `let q: Map<Bool, Bool> = m` compiles with no diagnostic under both `gunbc run` and `gunbc compile --target rust`.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, two links in one rule chain: v1.compiler.infer declared_type_conformance_diags_core ended `if !both_ground { [] }`, and conformance_ground_type admitted only kernel scalars and element collections whose first element is a kernel scalar, excluding keyed collections by name -- so every Map pair was accepted with no judgment; and v1.compiler.infer_types node_type_compatible's container arm compared `children |> first`, so every argument after the first was never compared even where the pair was judged. The one-peel leaves beside it (declared_type_kernel_inhabitance_mismatch_at_element, callable_element_signature_mismatch) each stated their own depth-one narrowing.",

    "RUNG: found BELOW the ladder -- accepted and emitted with no diagnostic.",

    "CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed: the source can still write the mismatch, and the compiler can refuse every one whose positions are established, because two applications of one template compare positionally on a finite type tree. A position holding an unsolved type variable is not decided by this judgment; it is a counted undecided cause, never an agreement, and a concrete disagreement at a sibling position still refuses.",

    "CLIMB (2026-11-01, gunbc#15595): v1.compiler.infer application_pair and application_arguments_inhabitance, consumed at declared_type_conformance_diags_core, inside declared_type_inhabitance and at the record-literal field chain; the four one-peel leaves were deleted. The first execution (kh-q2-regen2, head 3dd5e7c60442) passed 12 of 13 and found the record-literal field RED accepted, because that chain answered node_type_compatible by head before any per-argument arm; routing it through declared_type_obligation_diags made it 13 of 13. RESIDUAL: positions with no obligation producer (map value, variant payload, cast target, callable return) are outside this row.",

    "REVIEW TELL: a declared-type judgment that reads `children |> first`, peels exactly one level, or excludes a collection kind by name and returns an empty diagnostic list for what it excluded.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
